// The claim check stores claims in a hash set that rehashes as it fills, so a
// collision must still be caught when the two claimants are separated by enough
// intervening declarations to move the first one between buckets several times.
// The colliding pair here is the same `a_`/`b` vs `a`/`_b` boundary case as
// underscore_boundary_collision_err, split by ~200 unrelated claims.
